  guideSearchCopy: "A waiting search used to die after a short silence, while the screen still said it was looking. A second tab in the same browser was rejected outright, so two windows could not meet. After a few skips, a proof-of-work check was often too hard to finish. Those are fixed: a live search stays in the queue, a vanished search is started again, a second tab can join the waiting person when nobody else is queued, and the admission check is small enough to finish. If the other side never opens the live connection, the chat does not sit on “Connecting” forever.",
